    "prompt": "Create a new pixel-art game animation sheet for Urshifu, using this image as the exact identity, palette, camera and layout reference. Transparent background, exactly eight columns and four rows, wide empty transparent gutters; no text, no scenery, no effects. Preserve all anatomy, form and visible parts.\nEach row has a fixed camera: row1 SOUTH/front (face visible), row2 EAST/right profile (points right), row3 NORTH/rear (back visible, face hidden), row4 WEST/left profile (points left). Never turn the character toward the camera during an animation. The NORTH row must show only the back; do not draw a front face there.\nColumns1-4: four distinct, expressive flinch poses for a cartoon game impact: surprised wince, lowered head with tense/braced body, sustained closed-eye wince, return to ready stance. Columns5-8: four distinct resting-on-ground poses: knees/body lower, limbs fold as body settles sideways/down, fully flat with closed eyes, final still-flat resting pose. Last two columns must clearly show a prone body on the ground, with characteristic wings/tails/flower/markings intact. This is a nonviolent family video game: no injury, blood, wounds or damage marks. Keep consistent pixel scale, hard-edged pixel clusters and limited original palette. Each full-body sprite must be complete and remain inside its cell. Actual redraws of body and limbs rather than rotated or resized standing copies.",
